meta {
  name: Report entry
  type: http
  seq: 35
}

post {
  url: {{api}}/entries/{{partnerEntryId}}/report
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

script:pre-request {
  // A new key on every send: a retry of one send is then the same report, never a second (doc 06 section 1).
  req.setHeader("Idempotency-Key", require("uuid").v4());
}

body:json {
  {
    "reason": "OTHER",
    "detail": "A made-up detail, for trying the route."
  }
}

docs {
  Reports your partner's entry, with its photo and voice note, to a person who reviews it (FR-100, ADR-0053). 201 with the report's id, the entry's and the reason. The reason is NON_CONSENSUAL, MINOR_SEXUAL_CONTENT, VIOLENCE_OR_SELF_HARM, HARASSMENT or OTHER, exactly as written; anything else is 422. The detail is optional, what the reviewer should know, at most 500 characters.

  From the moment it is filed, the entry's photo and voice note are held back from you: run Today and they are PROCESSING. Your partner is shown them NOT_SHARED and is told nothing else, ever. The words stay. A person then dismisses the report (the media is shown again) or upholds it (it is deleted, or blocked).

  Run Days first, which keeps your partner's entry of the newest day as partnerEntryId. Your own entry is 409 REPORT_ON_OWN_ENTRY; anything you were never shown is 404. A reported entry that has since been deleted is still accepted, and so is a report after the bond has ended. Ten a day; the eleventh is 429.
}
